inotify-tools: make the install hook idempotent

The upstream install-exec-hook creates the fsnotifywait/fsnotifywatch symlinks
with a bare $(LN_S), which fails with "File exists" whenever Build/Install runs
a second time over a PKG_INSTALL_DIR that already has them. That happens on any
rebuild that re-enters the install step without a clean -- and in particular on
the -j1 diagnostic retry after a parallel build failure, where it masks the real
error with an unrelated one.

$(LN_S) is `ln -s`, so -f makes it replace rather than refuse. The package sets
PKG_FIXUP:=autoreconf, so patching Makefile.am is sufficient; Makefile.in and
Makefile are regenerated from it.

Verified: the inner patch applies cleanly to the pinned 4.25.9.0 tarball, and
this outer patch applies cleanly to the packages feed at master.

diff -ruN feedA/utils/inotify-tools/patches/110-idempotent-install-hook.patch feedB/utils/inotify-tools/patches/110-idempotent-install-hook.patch
--- a/utils/inotify-tools/patches/110-idempotent-install-hook.patch	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/utils/inotify-tools/patches/110-idempotent-install-hook.patch	2026-08-25 16:57:41.165113482 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+--- a/src/Makefile.am
++++ b/src/Makefile.am
+@@ -22,8 +22,8 @@ endif
+ 
+ install-exec-hook:
+ 	cd $(DESTDIR)$(bindir) && \
+-	$(LN_S) inotifywait fsnotifywait && \
+-	$(LN_S) inotifywatch fsnotifywatch
++	$(LN_S) -f inotifywait fsnotifywait && \
++	$(LN_S) -f inotifywatch fsnotifywatch
+ 
+ uninstall-hook:
+ 	rm -f $(DESTDIR)$(bindir)/{fsnotifywait,fsnotifywatch}
